--- !u!114 &691810699
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 691810697}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UnityEngine.UI::UnityEngine.UI.Text
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0.91194963, g: 0.8851712, b: 0.13478494, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 10102, guid: 0000000000000000e000000000000000, type: 0}
    m_FontSize: 25
    m_FontStyle: 1
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 0
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 1
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "How gameplay works:\n\nUse WASD to move squirrel up left down right respectively.
    \n\nCollect as much acorns as you can. \n\nOnce the squirrel is full of acorns,
    you must deposit into the hole.\n\nDon't get captured by the serpentine Jormungandr\n\nPress
    enter to skip text and lore\n\nThe Nut Collector:\n\nA long\u2026 long time ago,
    before time itself, The Lone God separated the heavens from the earth with nothing
    but their bare hands. But when faced with the emptiness of space, THEY severed
    one of THEIR arms, casting it down to the void below. From this arm grew the
    mighty Supreme Tree of Life\u2014Yggdrasil.\n\nFrom the blood of the Lone God,
    Yggdrasil birthed the cycles of the world, and from their breath came the acorns.
    And so, the squirrels were born, tasked with guarding the tree and its bounty.
    But deep beneath Yggdrasil, an ancient force stirred. The Jormungandr, a dark
    being born of the tree\u2019s shadows, rose against the first inhabitants of
    the world.\n\nThus, a great war raged between the squirrels and the Jormungandr,
    and the fate of Yggdrasil was sealed. To punish the Jormungandr\u2019s defiance
    of the natural order, the Lone God transformed them into the form of a snake\u2014forever
    bound to the roots of the tree, a symbol of their rebellion.\n\nAs the Lone God
    ascended to the heavens, THEY decreed that Yggdrasil would one day face Ragnarok.
    To survive the coming calamity, the squirrels must gather every acorn from Yggdrasil
    and deposit it into the tree, to prepare for Fimbulvinter\u2014the coldest winter
    the world has ever known.\n\nAnd so, the squirrels chose one among their kind,
    the bravest and most cunning of them all\u2014Ratatoskr. It is you, Ratatoskr,
    The Nut Collector, who must embark on this perilous journey to save your world,
    collect the sacred acorns, and face the serpentine wrath of the Jormungandr\u2026
    before time runs out."
